# Commands that stay on dev: watchers and servers, and what needs dev's display. Commands
# that use a store kept on the remote's disk are config/remote-store-commands. One entry per
# line: argv[0]'s basename, optionally followed by the arguments that must come next
# (`cargo watch`).
# Options may come before or between an entry's words (`cargo +nightly watch`, `hugo -D server`).
# A package manager's dev, start, serve, watch or preview script, also as the first `:` or
# `-` part of one, or watch as any part (`npm run dev`, `pnpm dev:web`, `npm run test:watch`,
# `yarn workspace web dev`; not `build:dev`), a
# task runner's task of exactly those names or with watch as a `-` part (`make build dev`, `just dev`, `deno task dev`,
# `turbo dev`, `nx serve web`, `nx run-many -t serve`), a listed program it runs
# (`npx vite`, `pnpm vite`, `uv run vite`, `uvx mkdocs serve`, `pipx run vite`, `python -m uvicorn`),
# and any command given --watch, --watchAll, --watch-*, --hot, --reload or --serve (not
# `=false`), or -w to tsc, rollup, webpack, mocha, vitest, tailwindcss, hugo or vite, match
# without an entry
# (watchServeMatch);
# `vite build` and `vite optimize` do not match vite. A best effort: a
# server or watcher it misses runs on the remote; `--where local` keeps one here.
# `--where <host>` overrides this list.
